atha dvādaśaḥ|
sahasrāṇīti atra bāhvoriti dvivacanamapi vakṣitaṃ bāhuṣvityarthaḥ| he bhagavaḥ (p.97a,f.93b,1st line)
tava bāhvo yadvā anantabāhoriti pratyekaṃ dhanurbāṇavyāpṛtatatbāhudvayābhiprāyeṇa(2nd line)
dvivacanaṃ hetayaḥ| āyudhāni sahasrāṇi sahasradhā ca vidyate ānantyavāci sahasraśabdaḥ|(3rd line)
dhanuḥ khaḍgaśūlimityevaṃ vijātīyaśarmasvarūpabhedena anantāni teṣvapi ekaika asminnaneka(4th line)
bhedāt anantaparakārīṇītyarthaḥ śrūyate hi| śūlāt śūlasahasrāṇi niṣpatantyasya tejaseti(5th line)
tāsāñca hetīnāṃ mukhāni parācīnā nikrudhi asmattaḥ|(6th line)
parārbha(ṅ)mukhāni kuru| yatasvamīśānaḥ sarveśvaraḥ prayuktānām apyupasaṃhāre śakto'sīti bhāvaḥ|(7th line)
asya mantrasya nārada ṛṣiḥ| śrī rudro devatā|
sarvapāpaharaṃ devaṃ sarvābharaṇabhūṣitam| 
sarvāyudhadharaṃ (*)dhyāyet sarvaloke maheśvaram|| iti|(*)(8th line)
upadravaparihārapradhānoyaṃ mantraḥ| ekakṛcchra(p.97b,f.94a,1st line)
cāraṇapūrvakam| sahasrajapānmantra(-) siddhiḥ| daśame anuvāke bhagavān (2nd line)
